<tr bgcolor=#F5DEB3><td colspan=2 align=center valign=middle>The Brainless Blonde Bombshell Bard</td></tr>
<tr bgcolor=#F5DEB3><td colspan=2 align=left valign=middle>"I'll never play a bard," I used to say, "they're too fiddly, it would drive me up the wall keeping track of songs I'm twisting and so on..."<br><br>
Ah, how wrong I was.  Late one night, having nothing better to do, I decided to just try one out, then delete her and start a "real" character...several hours later she was level three and I was in a deep discussion with bardish friends about twisting.<br><br>
As Magpye is my outer child, Sofew is my outer diitz.  She's somewhat brainless, she does stupid things, she's more concerned with looking cool then with having good stats...hence the dyed FS plate armor and the Blade of Passage (pretty, but not a terribly good weapon).<br><br>
And yet...she also has a half-decent weapon to use for "real" fighting.  That FS has pretty decent AC, and she has some nice stat pieces in her non-visible slots.  She's already collecting the coins for the Nostrolo tamborine quest.  For a rarely played character, she's leveling pretty decently...and you know, twisting, and figuring out what songs to twist in what patterns for different situations, is kind of fun.<br><br>I think she may be a keeper.<br><br>
</td></tr>
